-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+- Every rejection caught during a turn calls `onError` once with an `Error`: an existing `Error` is passed as the same instance, while any other value (including a string, plain object, or `undefined`) is wrapped with the original value as its `cause`. Both caller entry points preserve the original rejection unchanged ([validated by: reports every rejection as an Error while preserving the original caller rejection](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
